  "title": "Lemma B: if Z on ℝ^P vanishes off a compact K ⊆ U and Z|_U is integer multiplicity, then so is Z",
  "statement": "Let P, q ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P open, K ⊆ U compact, and Z ∈ D_q(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ q) with Z(ω) = 0 for every ω ∈ D^q(ℝ^P) whose tsupport is disjoint from K. Suppose Z|_U := Z.restrictDomain (subset_univ U) is an integer multiplicity current in U. That is, Z|_U = τ(M, θ, ξ) on D^q(U) for a rectifiable triple with IsRectifiableTriple U q M θ ξ and θ(x) ∈ ℕ for x ∈ M. Then Z is an integer multiplicity current in ℝ^P (IsIntegerMultiplicity Z, with a triple relative to univ).",
  "lean_statement": "∀ (P q : ℕ) (U K : Set (Eucl P)), IsOpen U → IsCompact K → K ⊆ U → ∀ Z : GeometricCurrentOn (univ : Set (Eucl P)) q, (∀ ω : TestFormOn (univ : Set (Eucl P)) q, Disjoint (tsupport (ω : DifferentialForm (Eucl P) q)) K → Z ω = 0) → IsIntegerMultiplicity (Z.restrictDomain (subset_univ U)) → IsIntegerMultiplicity Z",
  "lean_name": "fiw_tb_ext_isIntegerMultiplicity",
